sock_create_kern takes the network namespace from current->nsproxy->net_ns.
Use in_aton() to convert the dotted IP string to a __be32 address and htons()
for the port. The kvec wraps a pointer and length; the msghdr can be zeroed.
kernel_sendmsg takes the socket, the msghdr, the kvec, count of vecs, and total
length. Check every return value and release the socket on any failure path.
